          "answer": "**Go to an emergency department now. Do not wait for a routine appointment.** Spotting with a sharp pain on one side and shoulder-tip pain, at 7 weeks of pregnancy, needs same-day emergency assessment. A possible ectopic pregnancy (a pregnancy developing outside the womb) is the main concern to rule out, and it needs a doctor to examine you in person.\n\nThe urgency tool returned \"routine\" because none of its fixed rules matched your exact wording. I am not relying on that result. The emergency guidance I retrieved states that abdominal or pelvic pain in pregnancy with bleeding, faintness or shoulder-tip pain should be treated as an emergency (source: *Acute abdominal pain that needs urgent assessment*, surgical and emergency medicine guidance). You have bleeding and shoulder-tip pain, so I am escalating this.\n\n**Call emergency services immediately if you have any of these:**\n- Heavy bleeding, or bleeding that is increasing\n- Fainting, or feeling dizzy or faint\n- Pain that is getting worse\n- Pain that spreads across your abdomen\n- Fever, a racing heartbeat, or confusion (same source)\n\nDo not wait to see if the symptoms settle. If you have any of these signs, get emergency help straight away.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
